  "rationale": "D4, data-informed revision on the fourth-generation droplet forward. The laws of D3 stand: a train-only error anatomy found the rate plateau and both extinction clocks unbiased, 39 % of the train error in tracker artefacts, and the bands too wide at short leads. Changed: the radiative class is sharper around the critical diameter (five train droplets near it all went out radiatively and were given 0.5-0.75); heat-up is slower at 1 atm; the measurement band is 8 um instead of 20 um and the rate spread 0.08/0.05 instead of 0.10/0.06; and a broad component is mixed in when the prefix itself shows an unstable tracker (frames dropped by the validity gate, a prefix D0 far from the sheet's, D^2 growing). Every number typed by the author; no fit, no search; nothing chosen from validation.",
  "origin": "system"
}
